/// `exact-distributions`: Finite distributions with exact weights.
/// Implemented: a distribution holds exact rational weights in one canonical order. `distributes` states the exact distribution of a definition's runs over every answer of its draws, across worlds and sessions between seats. std's seeded generator, universal hashing and one-time pad each state theirs.
/// Not implemented: the corpus states no probability sheaf over an atomic site and no conditioning across the worlds of a run.
///
/// - owes: #6120
// One draw of one fair bit gives 0 and 1, each with weight one half. The
// corpus runs `bit` twice, once for each answer of its draw. The model
// source `draws.gandr` sums two draws of two bits.
//
// - see: `../../model/probability/draws.gandr`

// The host interface of randomness.
import std.rand;

/// One draw of one bit: 0 and 1, each with weight one half.
@[ distributes(("1/2 0", "1/2 1")) ]
def bit() -> [std.rand.Eff] Integer =
  std.rand.draw 1
